# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/

# Claude Code
.claude/

# Checkpoints (transient, resumable state)
*_checkpoint.json
tag_review_queue.json

# SQLite database (binary; its contents are in git as text under DB/dump/)
# Exception: GitHub Pages builds to docs/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
!docs/

# Source-fidelity audit: rendered crops and per-page working files
reports/source_audit_2026-11/work/

# The packet for community review: built files gather the held-back vocabulary in one readable place.
# Build them with scripts/build_review_packet.py (see community_review/README.md).
community_review/review_packet.html
community_review/review_packet.pdf
community_review/response_sheet.csv

# The catalogue of further sources as the owner brought it (2026-11-15): a spreadsheet with notes addressed to
# the owner and an e-mail address. Its content is in sources/catalogue.json, without the address
# (scripts/sources_catalogue.py). The spreadsheet stays on this computer.
/Skiri Pawnee Language Sources.xlsx

# Letters asking for permission and review, drafted for the owner to send. Private correspondence.
community_review/letters/

# Two books of ceremony found in docs/ on 2026-11-15 (Fletcher, The Hako; Murie, Ceremonies of the Pawnee, part 1).
# docs/ is the published site: anything committed there is public. The register of sources holds both back
# as ceremonial until the Pawnee Nation has said what may be shown (sources/README.md). No PDF belongs in docs/
# except the two printables, which sit in docs/printables/.
/docs/*.pdf

# Engines review: the per-form records hold thousands of forms the engines computed, most of them wrong.
# They are made again in a minute by scripts/engines_review/run_all.py. The test sets (attested forms only),
# the summaries and the Stage 1 trace are kept.
reports/engines_review/data/*.jsonl
